<span class="chapter-number">
                        INTRODUCTION
                    </span>
<h2>
                        Memory Management and Virtual Memory
                    </h2>
<p>
                        Memory management and virtual memory are important parts
                        of an operating system. They help a computer organize,
                        control, and use its memory properly while running
                        different programs and applications.
                    </p>
<p>
                        Every time a user opens a browser, plays a game,
                        edits a document, or runs a program, the computer
                        needs memory to store information required by that activity.
                    </p>
<p>
                        Memory management controls how memory is assigned,
                        used, monitored, and released. Virtual memory allows
                        a computer to use secondary storage as additional
                        support when available RAM is insufficient.
                    </p>
<div class="note">
<strong>Example:</strong>

                        When a student opens a browser, a document editor,
                        and a programming application, the operating system
                        manages their memory requirements.

                    </div>
</section>
